From 2d3009dc4bb8bd480d15ee86abd770118cf9834c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:36:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] input: Adds support for virtual-keyboard-unstable-v1
 protocol.

Creates the virtual keyboard manager in the input manager, and adds new
virtual keyboards through the same path as other keyboards. To have them
work with their own keymap:

* wlmim_keyboard_configure() does not replace the keymap of a virtual
  keyboard with the configured one.
* A keyboard without keymap is not made the seat's keyboard on creation,
  as that would send an empty keymap to the focused client.
* handle_key() sets the event's keyboard as the seat's keyboard before
  forwarding the key, so that the event is interpreted with the matching
  keymap when multiple keyboards are present. This is a no-op for a single
  keyboard.

Used by on-screen keyboards, wtype and remote desktop servers.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
